<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Pope Leo embarks on Latin America trip with a first stop in Uruguay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6876fced35e63713d7dfd9b7ecec6b1d9313ecb6dbaae30deedbf0f4cffe456a</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T14:58:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-pope-leo-embarks-on-latin-america-trip-with-a-first-stop-in-uruguay" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV is kicking off a three-nation tour of Latin America on Friday, November 6, with a visit to Uruguay, the region’s least Catholic and most secular country, three weeks after undergoing lung cancer surgery that had put the entire trip into question. After Uruguay, he will then go to Argentina and Peru. FRANCE 24's Hanna Roberts has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>California governor to grant clemency to all 548 death row inmates in state</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f16339044fc3f254e5fc86d125c669d6dade9a87ba61cb9e89b624bf1f129bf6</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T14:54:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-california-governor-to-grant-clemency-to-all-548-death-row-inmates-in-state" /><summary type="html">California's governor Gavy Newsom announced Thursday that he will commute all death sentences in the state to life without the possibility of parole. He said that "capital punishment is morally wrong." The state Supreme Court will have the final say in hundreds of those cases.</summary></entry><entry><title>The women who rode the blue wave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a12166109143df7c1ab07eb91e3efb15c1e4b21c8f3b878bb358c6f696450eb0</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T14:15:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261106-the-women-who-rode-the-blue-wave" /><summary type="html">In this edition, we report on how the US midterms, which saw the Democrats make massive gains, also marked a series of historic firsts for women. Also the dark side to Bangkok's booming fertility industry, which attracts thousands of foreign patients seeking assistance from the Thai capital's state-of-the-art private clinics. Plus how an impoverished neighbourhood in El Salvador, once a no-go zone plagued by gang violence, is being transformed by women into a vibrant canvas for street art.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Trump’s stillborn diesel deal: Why Russian oil tankers are not heading to the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d45d7679e825ea8b0086420493581b0dbb2f9d01dd8dced6baba166dbdcfc15</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:38:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-stillborn-diesel-deal-why-russian-oil-tankers-are-not-heading-to-the-us" /><summary type="html">The first oil tankers scheduled to deliver Russian diesel to the US under a deal between President Donald Trump and his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin have changed course and are no longer heading toward the US coast. It spells the end of an agreement announced with great fanfare before the midterms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future in question after midterms setback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab9b8ec0880b10ba0c058bcdad2f47609708a636b11cc945d3d504c536e8f6e0</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:15:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-us-defence-secretary-pete-hegseth-s-future-in-question-after-midterms-setback" /><summary type="html">US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future is in question after Tuesday's, November 3, midterms setback. On Thursday, November 5, he issued a video message vowing to fight efforts in Congress to impeach him and defending the ‌Iran war as “courageous and historic”. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech giants lose $1 trillion in one day after Democrats victory in midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6307d04439ee0e9d6667f0133086c812c7125f848e9f5ad027503a4f501293b7</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:15:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-tech-giants-lose-1-trillion-in-one-day-after-democrats-victory-in-midterms" /><summary type="html">Trillions of dollars have been wiped off the stock value of major tech firms in the US, Europe and Asia. Investors appear worried about the possibility of an AI slowdown and tougher regulation as Democrats won the midterms in the US. Some of the Democratic candidates had expressed their opposition to the data centres that are needed to power AI technology.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canada PM Mark Carney unveils budget to strengthen economy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:053a85621330b399e09f1fed22464e12c7a73727225eec1b32c3096604f076c7</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:10:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-canada-pm-mark-carney-unveils-budget-to-strengthen-economy" /><summary type="html">Canada's Prime Minister Mark Carney unveiled his first ever budget on November 5, which set out strong ambitions for greater economic independence from the US. The "Masters of our Destiny" budget also announced generous measures for parts of the economy affected by tariffs, setting aside 44 billion Canadian dollars for impacted businesses and workers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Democratic Party introduce a new 'New Deal'? Key narrative must be 'focused on economic issues'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53311c2052f385969114d0effbe434d13c8ab0327d8420591bac2a35591a4066</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:07:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/will-democratic-party-introduce-a-new-new-deal-key-narrative-must-be-focused-on-economic-issues" /><summary type="html">With Democrats poised to control both chambers of Congress, the party faces a defining challenge: how to constrain Donald Trump's presidency while carving out a path to the White House in 2028. For Ian Reifowitz, Distinguished Professor of History at SUNY Empire State University, the answer lies in drawing on the historical legacy of Franklin D. Roosevelt's New Deal coalition. Republicans, he argues, have progressively shifted electoral competition towards questions of identity, immigration and cultural conflict. Democrats, by contrast, must recover their traditional strength on economic security, affordability and everyday living standards. "These Democrats across the country ran on affordability." And that's how they must govern, explains Reifowitz.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Period of uncertainty: Trump is tormented, he's unstoppable, and he's desperate for immortality'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2335871f3124ba34a334eece0f0f901db1eb621a0d67116aec3f91bba6f8fc8</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:46:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-period-of-uncertainty-trump-is-tormented-he-s-unstoppable-and-he-s-desperate-for-immortality" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Craig Copetas, Greek-American author, international affairs columnist and editor at Türkiye Today and French Senator Hélène Conway-Mouret. “What you have is a tormented and unstable president who's desperate for immortality.” With this arresting assessment, Copetas captures what he considers the defining paradox of Donald Trump's presidency in the aftermath of the US midterm elections: a leader politically neutered at home but potentially emboldened on the international stage.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>California governor says commuting all death sentences in state</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18bcecd1b4912c84a2de57410963474ab4e89e166776f0abf284829f2c0e2711</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:05:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-california-governor-says-commuting-all-death-sentences-in-state" /><summary type="html">California Governor Gavin Newsom said Thursday, November 5, he was commuting all death sentences across the state to life imprisonment, in a move that will affect over 500 prisoners. FRANCE 24's correspondent Wassim Cornet reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: European stocks plunge after US midterm election results shock markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dba4b451b1b86dd1bc96d5e8a8bfba7ea2e79941baa2fcfc4ccba231f7588c45</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T09:37:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-live-european-stocks-plunge-after-us-midterm-election-results-shock-markets" /><summary type="html">European shares tumbled on Friday as global investors grappled with uncertainty over AI stocks, following the Democrats’ sweeping victory in the US midterm elections. The drop is partly due to fears that Democrats could curb the development of AI data centres, which are widely unpopular among US voters. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump calls midterms 'crooked', demands Alaska votes go to Republican candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6276d357ba53d49c018e0eb5d777a0718e6b2a46788c214347f5f653ee159c1</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-calls-midterms-crooked-demands-alaska-votes-go-to-republican-candidate" /><summary type="html">Despite having previously accepted the US midterm election results, President Donald Trump told reporters on Thursday the elections were "crooked", and he demanded the remaining votes for Alaska go to its incumbent Republican senator.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Leaders all over the world understand that Trump is only there for two more years &amp; then he's gone'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ea5ee0f039ccf98a6248b342e201a9b2eb32e661dd7b745acf073e05468761c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T07:08:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-leaders-all-over-the-world-understand-that-trump-is-only-there-for-two-more-years-then-he-s-gone" /><summary type="html">In American politics, even presidential power has its limits. And now, the laws of political gravity may finally be catching up with Donald Trump's hyper-aggressive exercise of executive authority. Following what political scientist Ian Bremmer describes as the most consequential electoral reversal for a governing party in more than half a century, the president and founder of Eurasia Group and GZERO Media argues that the United States has entered a new political phase: the beginning of the end of Trump's ability to dominate the political agenda, at home and on the world stage.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio denies plans to resign, says working for Trump until end of term has 'always been my plan'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:406db72de6b0dbaa300eb792a1beb98aec77f489255c7b10cd35d6051d3ee6e8</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T00:24:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-marco-rubio-denies-resignation-2028-white-house--dd09aa774082.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-marco-rubio-denies-resignation-2028-white-house" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio dismissed reports on Thursday that he planned to leave the administration after Republican midterm losses, telling The New York Times he intended to serve through the end of President Donald Trump’s term. Rubio, a potential 2028 presidential candidate, declined to discuss his plans.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Inhumane punishment': Governor Gavin Newsom to commute all 548 California death sentences</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adc20f7df7a9481c40a82e3e5cde0350bd6d7d330153f524218f8542cba45f19</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T19:59:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-inhumane-punishment-california-governor-gavin-newsom-to-commute-548-death-sentences--058895c955cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-inhumane-punishment-california-governor-gavin-newsom-to-commute-548-death-sentences" /><summary type="html">California Governor Gavin Newsom on Thursday said he would commute all 548 death sentences in the state to life in prison without parole, marking a major step away from capital punishment as he prepares to leave office after eight years.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Paraguay's president Peña impeached after resigning over banking scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:496425ea2a7e3293be4849e25f8226cf77e902a512a47e683054932237e95aad</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:33:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-paraguay-s-president-pe_a-impeached-moments-after-resigning-amid-banking-scandal--498613eca0a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-paraguay-s-president-pe%C3%B1a-impeached-moments-after-resigning-amid-banking-scandal" /><summary type="html">Paraguay’s Senate on Friday said it would not delay an impeachment trial against President Santiago Peña after a bank linked to him blocked millions of people – including pensioners – from accessing their money. Peña attempted to resign over the scandal on Thursday and then on Friday requested to delay the trial by three days, both of which were denied by the government.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: 'Donald Trump's wings have been more than clipped'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e7ce1e013d3d8612f057dcf57a613ff98a732799d3a2b58fc40886c33cb6598</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:46:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-donald-trump-s-wings-have-been-more-than-clipped--c82ffc4a0687.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-donald-trump-s-wings-have-been-more-than-clipped" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump faced a radically transformed and hostile political landscape after Democrats seized both the House of Representatives and the Senate in Tuesday's (November 3) midterms. The result was a personal humiliation for the 80-year-old Trump, leaving him as a lame duck president for the remaining two years of his term. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Identity crisis': Can Democrats 'deliver' following their 'historic', once in a generation victory?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35c630b39aba4b52f4b3990ae256ccb7a1f5fd84b9bf8cbd1637a3c1ebb15514</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:27:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/identity-crisis-can-democrats-deliver-following-their-historic-once-in-a-generation-victory--c1d1ab999d50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/identity-crisis-can-democrats-deliver-following-their-historic-once-in-a-generation-victory" /><summary type="html">A historic Democratic electoral breakthrough has transformed the American political landscape. For Laurie Dundon, Senior Associate Fellow at the European Leadership Network and former US diplomat, the central question is whether the Democratic Party can convert electoral momentum into coherent governance. "Can they deliver?" Dunden examines the apparent disintegration of Donald Trump's 2024 MAGA coalition alongside the Democratic Party's continuing ideological struggle between its progressive and centrist wings. Ahead of 2028, Dunden cautions against seeing Trump as a lame duck: "Trump is never going to stop being Trump." The resulting struggle over congressional spending powers, presidential vetoes, tariffs and investigations promises to be a delicate dance to watch".</summary></entry><entry><title>Bent on leaving his mark: Trump's proposed 'Triumphal Arch' sparks backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:286a35ec510951df14199e492120fcc36f42cb7936d11256cd62341e7f5ab2f5</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:55:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261105-bent-on-leaving-his-mark-trump-s-proposed-triumphal-arch-sparks-backlash--73d727b96284.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261105-bent-on-leaving-his-mark-trump-s-proposed-triumphal-arch-sparks-backlash" /><summary type="html">Since his return to power, US President Donald Trump has been intent on reshaping the nation's capital Washington, seeking to leave his name and mark on it. After his involvement with the Kennedy Center, the White House ballroom and the Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool, Trump is now particularly keen on building a 250-foot (79-metre) "Triumphal Arch" – a project he claims is intended to honour the 250th anniversary of the United States.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>What comes next for Democrats after midterm election victory?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f1a057badafaeccc5e98029e6951073a4feb5baab22e04b3476fc6fc8f8e071</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:54:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-what-comes-next-for-democrats-after-midterm-election-victory--4f83f2ac02be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-what-comes-next-for-democrats-after-midterm-election-victory" /><summary type="html">With the US midterms over, Democrats are turning to what could become one of their most crowded and unpredictable presidential primaries in decades – a 2028 contest ​likely to expose the party's divide over how to win back the White House. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Farewell Botox, heels and big hair: Is this the end of MAGA women?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c60f5d8e322964793e5812495b16fe255b62774cce473a9d280a5b3bab966b26</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T12:15:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261105-farewell-botox-heels-and-big-hair-is-this-the-end-of-maga-women--6cd41e6c1263.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261105-farewell-botox-heels-and-big-hair-is-this-the-end-of-maga-women" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, November 5: "Loser" and "Reborn in the USA" are just some of the headlines dominating the international press after the Democrats stomped to victory in the US midterm elections. What impact will their success have on the rest of Donald Trump's presidency? How will he govern with a Democratic-controlled Congress? These are just some of the burning questions after that vote. Also, do the midterm results signal the end of the MAGA woman and the "Mar-a-Lago face"?</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Elon Musk fails $440 million bet as Republicans lose</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd76ac96186cf3e45ba1860d85efe33638235101a29ed4d48fa826168c372f84</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:29:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-elon-musk-fails-440-million-bet-as-republicans-lose--5fb12e38eb82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-elon-musk-fails-440-million-bet-as-republicans-lose" /><summary type="html">The 2026 midterm elections were the most expensive on record, with nearly 12 billion dollars spent during the campaign. Tech tycoon Elon Musk was by far the largest individual donor ever, injecting over 440 million dollars of his money to support the GOP. Tuesday's resounding Democratic victory showed the limits of his money, power and influence.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Democrats say ready to negotiate and promise big changes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e26f8f1c8ca61e0dc7f29ff3e1105416017bf679ab1c16541429e6611e73b6f</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:22:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-democrats-say-ready-to-negotiate-and-promise-big-changes--34ae17572d70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261105-us-midterms-democrats-say-ready-to-negotiate-and-promise-big-changes" /><summary type="html">US Democrats are promising to leverage their landslide election win to bring down living costs and hold President Donald Trump's administration to account. They are set to take control of both chambers of Congress in January, but delivering on their agenda could mean striking deals with the very president they have pledged to rein in.</summary></entry><entry><title>Melania Trump urges 'enduring' ceasefire at meeting with Ukrainian, Russian officials</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88ea86213eb94114e0806b743aa8fd26832530a65676db45d1014b0b488a7886</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T05:23:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-melania-trump-to-host-ukrainian-russian-officials-at-white-house--000b54c4acdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261105-melania-trump-to-host-ukrainian-russian-officials-at-white-house" /><summary type="html">Russian and Ukrainian officials, including human rights chiefs, met US First Lady Melania Trump at the White House on Thursday ahead of Abu Dhabi talks aimed at ending the Ukraine war. The meeting comes weeks after Melania Trump helped broker a partial ceasefire enabling the evacuation of civilians from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's second-term playbook: Fake news, AI and attacks on his critics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88234da33f38a21c67bf10c653694df3da9d28dafa283938316ff7a288de5abc</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:44:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261104-trump-s-second-term-playbook-fake-news-ai-and-attacks-on-his-critics--e29038ea0d3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261104-trump-s-second-term-playbook-fake-news-ai-and-attacks-on-his-critics" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump could be credited with popularising the term "fake news", but his own presidency has been riddled with numerous false claims, conspiracy theories and misleading content. In this special fact-checking segment, Vedika Bahl examines Trump's second term: his consistent attacks on political opponents, use of AI-generated images to glorify himself and push political narratives, and what happens when journalists challenge him.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Blue wave across America: Do US midterms signal beginning of the end for Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c05160392973d947556dc302d5528927abe525f566093812154715fbdd03123a</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T19:49:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261104-blue-wave-across-america-do-us-midterms-signal-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump--f1d9ca650a12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261104-blue-wave-across-america-do-us-midterms-signal-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump" /><summary type="html">He asked people to pretend he was on the ballot and they did. Voters across the United States have chased US President Donald Trump's Republican majorities from both houses of Congress. How big a landslide is this for the Democrats?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Democrats warn Trump camp to ‘lawyer up’ as anger over corruption drives midterms wipeout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b6cb0f0e2ee332a29e9600d6a66a391a634833425b6ad792ab2096d2357d37b</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T18:01:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-democrats-warn-trump-camp-lawyer-up-anger-over-corruption-drives-midterms-wipeout-gop--7b31d5ddc778.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-democrats-warn-trump-camp-lawyer-up-anger-over-corruption-drives-midterms-wipeout-gop" /><summary type="html">Corruption in government was high on the minds of US voters as they dealt US President Donald Trump’s party a chastening defeat in midterm elections, toppling Republican strongholds like dominoes and flipping both chambers of Congress. Triumphant Democrats have warned the Trump administration to “lawyer up”; how they go about tackling alleged graft and abuse of power could shape both their own fortunes and the country’s politics.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Once-in-a-generation event: Historic election a shocking repudiation of Trump &amp; the MAGA movement'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10893d80a1c0cc486484abe52eb78957863566aee2011642cfb4d728d6d7abe0</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:49:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/once-in-a-generation-event-historic-election-a-shocking-repudiation-of-trump-the-maga-movement--e99c6f8b95fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/once-in-a-generation-event-historic-election-a-shocking-repudiation-of-trump-the-maga-movement" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Adam Jentleson, President of the Searchlight Institute and author of Supermajority: How Democrats Can Build Lasting Power, For Jentleson, the Democrats' sweeping midterm victory represents far more than the familiar backlash against an incumbent president. "This is a once-in-a-generation event." But electoral breadth presents a governing dilemma. Can a coalition stretching from progressive reformers to culturally conservative Democrats translate its diversity into legislative action? "Pluralism is not just a political strategy. It is actually a moral good in a democracy," he insists. But electoral breadth presents a governing dilemma. Can a coalition stretching from progressive reformers to culturally conservative Democrats translate its diversity into legislative action? And can a party united by opposition to Trump sustain that unity when confronted with difficult choices over healthcare, immigration, economic inequality and climate change?</summary></entry><entry><title>European leaders welcome Democrats' US midterms election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32047be6f24ff1c62fc70ce658d799caa99c7aa90436fdb2dfa06eeb56c9a25e</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:00:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-welcome-democrats-us-midterms-election-win--9eb298186d7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-welcome-democrats-us-midterms-election-win" /><summary type="html">European leaders voiced hopes for a reset with the United States on Wednesday, November 4, after voters delivered a huge midterm election defeat to President Donald Trump and his Republican party. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms bring a wave of historic firsts as minorities win key races</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e063ae846495236a82443f7815d7a0e713169e32135256ccfb2c1f150f1d689</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:51:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-bring-a-wave-of-historic-firsts-as-minorities-win-key-races--466ff9f5f4fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-bring-a-wave-of-historic-firsts-as-minorities-win-key-races" /><summary type="html">US midterms bring a wave of historic firsts as minorities win key races: The first Native American female senator in Minnesota, the first openly gay male senator in New Hampshire, the first Muslim senator in Michigan and the country's first Black female governor in Georgia. FRANCE 24's Elitsa Gadeva has more.</summary></entry></feed>
